WEBVTT

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:05.560
Misha.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:07.680
I managed to get some time off work,

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:08.820
so do you want to go to a hot spring?

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.190
Too much trouble to go.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:14.120
But you get to have good food,

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:16.700
and relax in the hot water.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.760
I don't really need to relax,

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.540
and I can take a bath here at home.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.440
Also, the food that woman 
makes is pretty good.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.080
There's no real reason to go anywhere.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.380
It's a hot spring where you can 
take a bath with capybaras.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:34.260
You mean the capybaras 
hot spring in Hokkaido?!

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.840
They said their reservation 
book was full on TV!

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:41.140
Received Mail

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:41.140
Kaihara Inn
 Your Reservation
 Takanashi Yasuhiro

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:41.140
Your dad worked his magic!

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.080
Wow!

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:47.150
<i>Misha is looking at me 
with sparkles in her eyes!</i>

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:48.970
We're starting at 12 o'clock.

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:49.670
Right!

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:50.650
Understood.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:53.150
<i>I'm glad I worked so hard 
to get the reservation.</i>

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.340
Are we going, just the two of us?

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:57.070
Of course.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.570
<i>That means, for once in a long time,</i>

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:01.290
<i>I won't have to deal with that woman.</i>

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.100
Yasuhiro!

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:04.790
Thank you!

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:07.540
<i>I didn't expect her to be that overjoyed.</i>

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:11.050
Don't tell that woman about this at all!

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:12.040
That woman?

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:14.090
Oh, you mean the maid?

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:16.840
If the information manages 
to get to her somehow,

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:18.470
there's a possibility she'll 
come chasing after me.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:20.220
That wouldn't happen...

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.600
You don't know her ability to persevere.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:27.850
Milady!

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:30.720
She'll chase me to the ends of this earth.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:35.000
We can say I'm staying 
at Washiwashi's house,

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.690
and that since you're on vacation, 
she doesn't need to come for a while.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:40.870
That's fine,

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:44.760
but then we won't be able 
to get her a souvenir.

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:47.000
She's always working hard for us.

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:48.370
She doesn't need one!

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:50.380
R-Really?

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:54.280
Let's make this vacation 
a success, no matter what!

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.260
Without that woman around.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.140
S-Sure.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:32.520
<b>Episode 10:   My Maid And Yasuhiro</b>

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:36.580
This'll be the first time that Misha and 
I go on a trip alone since you've left us.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:39.400
I'll try to make sure she has a good time.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:41.450
<i>Misha.</i>

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.400
<i>This is Yasuhiro.</i>

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.200
<i>Hi, there.</i>

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:50.890
<i>I'm sorry. She gets shy around new people.</i>

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:52.700
<i>Can't expect her to accept me out of nowhere.</i>

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:57.330
<i>Nice to meet you, Misha-chan.</i>

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:58.130
<i>Hope we can get along.</i>

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:03.840
<i>Do you want to marry Mommy?</i>

00:04:04.150 --> 00:04:05.430
<i>Misha!</i>

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:06.310
<i>Yep.</i>

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.970
<i>If you allow me.</i>

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:11.830
<i>I don't mind living with you...</i>

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:15.900
<i>But any more than that...</i>

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:18.900
<i>That's fine.</i>

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:24.610
<i>Let's spend enough time together 
to become real friends.</i>

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:38.160
I think we're a lot closer 
compared to back then,

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:41.260
but I don't think she's 
called me "Daddy" once.

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:43.620
Sorry for being such a weak husband.

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:48.760
<b>Day of the trip</b>

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:48.760
For now, I'm going to head 
to Washiwashi's house.

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:51.030
Let's meet at the station at 9 o'clock.

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:52.470
You're being rather careful about this.

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:55.310
<i>We already had our luggage sent to the inn.</i>

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:58.370
<i>I asked Midorin to take care of 
Kumagoro and the others, too.</i>

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:00.250
<i>I didn't tell her where we're going.</i>

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:02.320
<i>She can't find us.</i>

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:07.460
I'm here, Yasuhiro.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:08.950
She's not here.

00:05:10.050 --> 00:05:10.830
Misha, take a—

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:11.770
She's not there.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.080
Not there.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.210
<b>Capybara</b>

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:14.000
Misha.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:14.700
Not over there.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.330
She's not here!

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:18.830
Excuse me.

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:20.340
Excuse me.

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:23.800
Excuse me.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:25.300
She is here!

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:30.880
I would like to welcome you to our inn.

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:34.050
My name is Kamoi. I'll be assigned 
to help you during your stay.

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:36.050
That is my real name, too.

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:37.100
We know that!

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:39.480
Why is our maid here?

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:44.600
I was free, so I was hoping to 
do a short term part-time job,

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:46.780
and when I went looking, 
I found this place.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:48.620
This is quite the coincidence.

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:50.680
Feels like fate to me.

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:51.620
<i>In reality,</i>

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:54.310
<i>I obtained the information from 
when the Miss and Washizaki-sama</i>

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:56.120
<i>were talking on the way home from school.</i>

00:05:56.480 --> 00:05:57.600
I want to go home.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.670
We just got here!

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:03.110
Also, we already know our maid, 
and she's serving us, so...

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:03.840
Oh, yeah.

00:06:04.360 --> 00:06:07.050
Sorry for not telling you.

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.720
Don't worry about it at all.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:12.980
I'm sure Milady just 
didn't want me to feel jealous.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:14.720
An inn such as this one flooded 
with a deluge of reservations—

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:17.700
of course I'd want to come along, too.

00:06:19.120 --> 00:06:22.580
I'm plenty happy, though. I get to be 
here with you as one of the waitstaff.

00:06:23.010 --> 00:06:25.760
I'm glad you feel that way.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:27.610
Don't say you want to go home, Misha.

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:30.720
We came all the way here to 
the capybara hot spring, so...

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:31.430
Oh, yeah!

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:32.240
There're capybaras!

00:06:34.010 --> 00:06:35.600
<i>This woman's annoying, but...</i>

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:38.790
<i>I do want to swim with those capybaras!</i>

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:43.250
<i>We might not get another chance 
to get a reservation, too.</i>

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:45.750
<i>I'll just have to live with this.</i>

00:06:46.580 --> 00:06:50.450
In any event, if you need anything at 
all, please do not hesitate to call me.

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:57.280
I'll be there to help you, twenty-four 
hours a day, anytime, anywhere.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:58.780
<i>That was scary!</i>

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:00.350
<b>Welcome to the Capybara Bath!</b>

00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:05.790
This is it!

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:06.550
Misha,

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:10.440
if you get out before I do, then 
go straight back to the room.

00:07:10.440 --> 00:07:12.110
Don't go off by yourself.

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:13.460
Okay!

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:23.380
It's time...

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:24.630
Capybara!

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:25.630
Capybara!

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:27.130
Capyba—

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:30.260
<i>Huh? Why is she here?</i>

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:32.980
<i>What should I do? Head back to the room?</i>

00:07:32.980 --> 00:07:34.450
<i>But...</i>

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:38.270
<i>I'm sure that was just an illusion 
I saw due to immense fear.</i>

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:52.990
<i>All right...</i>

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:54.150
<i>She's not here.</i>

00:07:54.150 --> 00:07:56.280
<i>And time for the capy... baras?</i>

00:07:57.140 --> 00:07:57.970
They're so far!

00:07:58.440 --> 00:08:01.630
Mommy, the capybaras are so small!

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:04.540
I thought we'd be taking a bath with them,

00:08:04.540 --> 00:08:07.020
but I guess they're behind a one-way mirror.

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:13.800
<i>Come forth.</i>

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:23.000
The capybaras are here!

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:23.940
You're right.

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:26.720
Why are so many of them collecting there?

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:28.820
It's almost like that 
girl asked them to come.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:32.220
They're so cute!

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:37.220
Khorosho!

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:38.330
Amazing!

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:42.070
You're great, Milady!

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:43.580
You're a capybara fairy!

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:46.600
That doesn't sound like you're trying 
to say something good about me...

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:48.590
Aren't you supposed to 
be attending the rooms?!

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.730
I took a lunch break.

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:55.440
I only need a small sliver 
of chocolate for food,

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:58.160
so I decided to ambush you.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:00.600
You shouldn't basically announce 
you're stalking people, you know?!

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:03.250
I haven't brought any cameras 
or anything like that in here,

00:09:03.250 --> 00:09:04.480
so there's no problem.

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:05.650
Why would you?!

00:09:05.650 --> 00:09:06.850
I'll never forget that scene!

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:08.440
No! Forget right now!

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:12.230
Huh? You're getting out?

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:15.150
You haven't soaked in the water at all.

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:16.820
Because you're here!

00:09:17.330 --> 00:09:19.740
<i>Plus if I head out to the yard, 
I'll get to pet the capybaras!</i>

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:22.030
You don't have to get so embarrassed—

00:09:22.030 --> 00:09:24.080
we're going to get married someday.

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:24.960
Stay in there forever!

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:30.810
<i>I was told not to walk around, 
but I'm just headed to the yard.</i>

00:09:30.810 --> 00:09:33.960
<i>I'm sure Yasuhiro's still in the bath, 
so there's no real problem, right?</i>

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:35.970
<b>Capybara Petting Grounds</b>

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:42.570
Capybaras in the flesh!

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:45.090
I get to touch their fur!

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:46.480
Huh?

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:52.230
A-A panda?

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:57.070
A wild panda?

00:09:57.390 --> 00:10:00.300
I saw it behind the petting area.

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:01.990
Misha, you went out alone?

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:05.080
Just for a little bit.

00:10:05.080 --> 00:10:06.550
Anyway, there was a panda!

00:10:06.550 --> 00:10:07.500
Isn't that cool?

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:08.750
Misha.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:10.500
Really excited, right?!

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:16.380
I don't think there are 
any wild pandas in Japan.

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:19.260
I know that, but I saw what I saw.

00:10:19.490 --> 00:10:23.200
You're just trying to put one over on me.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:23.890
No.

00:10:24.460 --> 00:10:26.000
There was a panda.

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:28.020
On the mountain behind the petting area.

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:30.020
Okay, okay.

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:33.150
You don't believe me, do you?

00:10:41.250 --> 00:10:43.580
That panda's bugging me.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:44.410
Yasuhiro...

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:46.910
Oh, he's asleep.

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:51.670
<i>Then this gives me a chance to get evidence!</i>

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:53.670
Actually, I just want to see the panda.

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:55.920
<b>Disappointment</b>

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:56.540
Pandas at the zoo basically are 
just sleeping all the time.

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:05.930
On no, I fell asleep!

00:11:06.670 --> 00:11:08.120
Great...

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:09.810
Misha, sorry—

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:12.710
Misha?

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:26.160
Excuse me.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:30.640
Dinner has been prepared.

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:31.540
Maid-san!

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:33.520
Misha isn't here!

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:34.880
I can't get a hold of 
her on her cell, either.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:36.460
I'm not getting any GPS data, either.

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:38.980
Milady has gone missing?

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:42.970
Please tell me every detail of the events

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:44.510
leading to Milady's disappearance.

00:11:44.840 --> 00:11:46.920
I'm sure she went to the mountain out back.

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:49.920
She was saying that there was a panda at the 
mountain behind the capybara petting area!

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:51.390
Please calm down.

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:55.020
We do not know if that's 
where she's gone yet.

00:11:55.360 --> 00:12:00.400
I want you to ask the other workers 
here, and have them search the inn.

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:02.910
What about you?

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:05.550
I'll go to the mountain to 
search for Milady.

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:06.580
Then I should go, too—

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:07.540
No.

00:12:08.550 --> 00:12:10.410
The sun has already set.

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.220
It's dangerous to head to the mountain.

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:13.790
Then it's no different from you going.

00:12:14.010 --> 00:12:15.280
Did you forget?

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:17.380
I was previously a Self Defense Force member.

00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:20.690
Yes, but I'm her father...

00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:22.260
And that's why you can't go.

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:25.080
You're the only parent she has left.

00:12:25.080 --> 00:12:27.140
If something happened to you 
out there on that mountain,

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:29.140
what would Milady do?

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:33.420
Isn't it also important for you 
to be here, safe and sound,

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:35.700
ready to welcome her back?

00:12:37.180 --> 00:12:38.350
I understand.

00:12:38.350 --> 00:12:39.900
I apologize for speaking out of turn.

00:12:41.630 --> 00:12:42.900
This is my fault.

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:48.750
If I only punished her properly for not 
coming straight back to the room.

00:12:49.590 --> 00:12:51.540
This wouldn't have happened.

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:55.020
She's a smart girl.

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:57.290
I'm sure she's fine, even if she 
did make her way onto the mountain.

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:00.840
If you don't find her after 
generally searching the inn,

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:02.670
then please go to the police.

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:06.290
It's possible she was kidnapped, as well.

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:11.720
<i>I talked up myself a second ago,</i>

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:15.770
<i>but I don't know much about 
mountain rescue, either.</i>

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:19.330
<i>After sunset, the temperature 
drops below freezing.</i>

00:13:19.330 --> 00:13:21.190
<i>I need to hurry.</i>

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:24.290
<i>Milady, please be safe.</i>

00:13:25.070 --> 00:13:28.070
<b>Two hours ago</b>

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:30.260
I don't think it went that far...

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:34.010
I'm hungry.

00:13:34.010 --> 00:13:36.130
Maybe I should just give up and go back.

00:13:36.130 --> 00:13:37.180
Um...

00:13:37.180 --> 00:13:38.840
Which way did I take to get here again?

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:42.420
I can just use the GPS on my phone 
and an app to figure out where I am.

00:13:43.270 --> 00:13:43.590
Huh?

00:13:43.930 --> 00:13:45.920
What?!

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:47.090
<i>I lost my smartphone!</i>

00:13:47.620 --> 00:13:48.590
Where is it?!

00:13:53.050 --> 00:13:54.100
No...

00:13:56.910 --> 00:14:00.360
I'm sure I'll be able to see the inn 
if I just get somewhere high enough.

00:14:00.770 --> 00:14:01.570
Jump.

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:05.360
<b>Can't climb trees at all!!</b>

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:09.800
<i>I'm not stranded here in the mountains, am I?</i>

00:14:10.630 --> 00:14:14.840
No, I'm just a kid. I'm sure 
I couldn't have walked far.

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:17.440
I'm sure the inn is close by.

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:20.430
I'll make it back if I just start walking.

00:14:20.430 --> 00:14:22.080
Yep, I'm sure I'll be fine.

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:29.930
The path forward has gotten 
harder to deal with.

00:14:31.480 --> 00:14:32.470
<i>It's cold.</i>

00:14:33.570 --> 00:14:35.580
<i>And it's dark now.</i>

00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:38.230
<i>I'm hungry.</i>

00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:40.600
Don't go off by yourself.

00:14:40.970 --> 00:14:43.860
This happened because
I didn't listen to Yasuhiro.

00:14:44.140 --> 00:14:48.860
<i>Maybe I'll die here,
if I can't make it back...</i>

00:14:51.150 --> 00:14:52.040
<i>I guess that's fine, too.</i>

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:54.700
<i>I'll get to see Mommy again.</i>

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:56.580
<i>Kumagoro...</i>

00:14:57.240 --> 00:14:59.440
<i>There's the hamsters, Big, 
Medium, and Small...</i>

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:01.260
<i>Yasuhiro...</i>

00:15:01.990 --> 00:15:03.110
<i>Washizaki...</i>

00:15:03.760 --> 00:15:05.500
<i>And even Morikawa-san.</i>

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:10.170
School was just getting fun, too...

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:11.930
I want to go home.

00:15:14.020 --> 00:15:16.110
Actually, maybe I'd rather die here.

00:15:16.110 --> 00:15:18.340
I won't have to see that woman again.

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:22.650
The panda!

00:15:23.080 --> 00:15:25.140
I knew you were here, Panda!

00:15:25.720 --> 00:15:26.650
So cute...

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:27.640
Huh?

00:15:27.400 --> 00:15:29.650
<b>Normal Panda</b>

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:29.650
You seem sorta skinny.

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:31.900
Maybe because you're a wild panda.

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:35.960
I lost my smartphone, so 
I can't take a picture.

00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:36.930
Too bad.

00:15:37.340 --> 00:15:39.850
Hey, do you know where the inn is?

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:41.150
You were there this afternoon, right?

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:44.130
So cute!

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:44.920
That's not what I should be doing.

00:15:45.170 --> 00:15:45.680
Um...

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:50.060
Maybe we can't communicate because 
you're not used to humans.

00:15:52.640 --> 00:15:57.560
But I might be able to get back 
to the inn if I just follow you.

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:02.840
A river.

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:05.950
I get the feeling we're getting 
further away from the inn.

00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:15.570
No, I can't eat that raw...

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:19.090
You're so cute, you know that?!

00:16:19.090 --> 00:16:20.330
What? Blood?!

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:23.620
<i>Do pandas eat fish?</i>

00:16:24.060 --> 00:16:27.210
<i>I read that they were originally 
carnivorous​ in this encyclopedia...</i>

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:31.170
<i>The panda's eating fish, and 
we're currently in Hokkaido...</i>

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:32.430
<i>Could this actually be a...</i>

00:16:33.220 --> 00:16:34.300
<i>A brown bear?!</i>

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:37.960
A-Are you a brown bear 
with panda-patterned fur?!

00:16:38.600 --> 00:16:40.520
Stop being so cute!

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:42.230
Your mouth has blood all over it, though.

00:16:42.680 --> 00:16:44.630
<i>I don't feel like I'm about to be attacked,</i>

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:45.800
<i>but will I be okay?</i>

00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:47.220
<i>It's still pretty small, too...</i>

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:51.740
<i>But if it's small then does that mean 
the mother's around here somewhere?</i>

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:59.370
No! I'm not causing any trouble!

00:17:01.390 --> 00:17:03.660
<i>I'm not getting through to 
her because of her rage.</i>

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:10.200
<i>I-I'm going to be killed!</i>

00:17:10.200 --> 00:17:11.700
<i>I'm dead this time!</i>

00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:14.940
M-Mommy!

00:17:14.940 --> 00:17:15.940
Milady!

00:17:16.770 --> 00:17:17.900
Don't move!

00:17:17.900 --> 00:17:19.760
You can't show your back to a bear!

00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:22.470
I'll head to you.

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:33.950
I'm here now.

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:36.140
Kamoi Tsubame is here to rescue you.

00:17:36.680 --> 00:17:38.950
Don't use the chaos of the 
situation to try to hug me!

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:42.670
I didn't expect you to refuse 
me in a situation like this.

00:17:42.670 --> 00:17:44.360
This didn't go as I imagined.

00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:46.540
I'll refuse you all year 
long, every single day!

00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:50.290
I feel better now that I see you're 
a lot more energetic than I expected.

00:17:56.090 --> 00:18:01.050
I'm going to return you to your 
father, no matter what it takes.

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:03.310
<i>Is she planning on fighting?</i>

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:05.930
<i>She's strong, but up against a bear...</i>

00:18:05.930 --> 00:18:06.940
<i>She'll die!</i>

00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:08.190
Stop it!

00:18:08.750 --> 00:18:11.080
My name is Kamoi Tsubame, 
twenty-eight years of age,

00:18:11.080 --> 00:18:14.320
and I love Milady 
with all my body and mind!

00:18:15.770 --> 00:18:19.560
I met the her on a chilling 
day, when it was snowing!

00:18:19.560 --> 00:18:21.380
I didn't need anyone and 
took care of myself,

00:18:21.380 --> 00:18:24.170
and yet her laughter pierced 
my ears just like a bell.

00:18:24.170 --> 00:18:26.800
My eyes found themselves looking 
in the direction of her voice,

00:18:26.800 --> 00:18:30.380
and there I saw, but what for a moment, 
looked like a snow fairy with silver hair,

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:31.440
eyes of jade,

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:32.590
skin like white porcelain,

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:34.240
and a sparkling smile!

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:36.600
A pure, young, and beautiful 
Russian girl lay before me!

00:18:36.600 --> 00:18:38.560
At that moment, a bolt of 
lightning pieced through me.

00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:41.600
Oh! For how even if this little girl, 
as ephemeral as the snow itself,

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:43.760
has her first period and 
no longer is a fairy,

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:45.100
I swore that I would still love 
her for the rest of my life,

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:47.270
and that I would protect her, 
even in exchange for my own life!

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:50.480
And if you try to get in the way of that,

00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:53.110
I will forced to demonstrate my vow to her!

00:19:03.430 --> 00:19:07.410
<i>The mother got so disgusted listening to 
that story, she lost the will to fight.</i>

00:19:07.810 --> 00:19:09.650
Looks like that worked out somehow.

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:12.790
I was betting that would 
make her lose the will to fight,

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:15.380
but it might have worked her up even more.

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:17.940
I'm glad no blood was spilled.

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:19.670
Milady?

00:19:19.960 --> 00:19:21.120
You're such a freak.

00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:21.760
I can't deal with you.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:25.530
Even though I risked my life to save yours?

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:28.640
Shouldn't you have fallen in love with 
me and asked for my hand in marriage?

00:19:28.890 --> 00:19:30.580
Yeah, but that was a disgusting 
way to save someone.

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:31.800
That'd never happen.

00:19:32.360 --> 00:19:33.550
There she is!

00:19:33.550 --> 00:19:34.610
She's safe!

00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:36.610
I'm safe!

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:38.960
Thank you for finding me!

00:19:38.960 --> 00:19:42.610
But I'm the one who saved you...

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:45.120
Misha!

00:19:46.230 --> 00:19:47.350
Yasuhiro!

00:19:52.610 --> 00:19:56.230
Misha, I told you not to 
go off by yourself, right?

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:58.800
I want you to keep your word.

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:01.170
I'm sorry.

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:02.430
Good girl.

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:07.680
Everyone, thank you for finding my girl.

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:11.740
My lack of supervision caused this ordeal.

00:20:12.310 --> 00:20:15.990
I apologize for the trouble this has caused.

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:18.070
I'm sorry.

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:19.070
I'm sorry.

00:20:19.430 --> 00:20:22.010
No, we're just glad she's safe.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:27.660
Kamoi-san, thank you for finding my daughter.

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:31.080
No, I just was doing my duty as your maid.

00:20:35.160 --> 00:20:36.960
Sorry for causing you trouble.

00:20:37.830 --> 00:20:39.210
Milady...

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:42.970
And... thank you...

00:20:45.700 --> 00:20:46.830
Let's get married!

00:20:46.830 --> 00:20:47.770
Never happening.

00:20:47.770 --> 00:20:48.490
Married?

00:20:48.490 --> 00:20:51.890
I'm sure it was cold out there, everyone.

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:53.560
I made some nice salmon and miso stew.

00:20:53.560 --> 00:20:55.270
Please come in and eat.

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:57.500
Let's at least get engaged!

00:20:57.500 --> 00:20:59.890
I want to eat the stew!

00:20:59.890 --> 00:21:01.270
Bleh...

00:21:01.720 --> 00:21:02.730
It was my first time...

00:21:02.730 --> 00:21:03.150
Huh?

00:21:03.640 --> 00:21:05.530
My first time scolding her.

00:21:06.430 --> 00:21:09.280
<i>You did it in a pretty soft way, though.</i>

00:21:12.600 --> 00:21:13.290
It's cold...

00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:14.900
Did you catch a cold?!

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:16.750
You were out in the cold this whole time.

00:21:17.320 --> 00:21:18.680
I'll turn up the temp.

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:22.310
Maybe I saw a blanket somewhere.

00:21:22.310 --> 00:21:22.710
Huh?

00:21:23.450 --> 00:21:25.120
Misha...

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:32.220
You don't have a fever...

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:38.480
You don't have a fever, but 
you're still pretty warm, Misha.

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:43.600
I'm really glad you're okay.

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:47.880
I wouldn't know what to 
do if I lost you, too.

00:21:49.460 --> 00:21:54.460
Misha, your mom left you to 
me, and you're precious to me.

00:21:54.980 --> 00:21:58.410
I can't go and save you like our maid,

00:21:58.410 --> 00:22:00.040
or maybe do that much at all,

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:02.450
but I'd like you to call me your Dad—

00:22:05.690 --> 00:22:08.790
Well, I guess there's no point in rushing it.
